    "final_answer": "I found the \"Resolve merge conflicts\" course in GitHub Skills. Here are the details:\n\n## Resolve Merge Conflicts Course\n\n**Repository:** `skills/resolve-merge-conflicts`\n**Description:** Learn why conflicts happen and how to resolve them.\n\n### Course Overview\nMerge conflicts happen when two people make changes to the same file on GitHub—a common occurrence when you're working with others. While resolving differences might involve some discussion, merge conflicts don't have to be scary.\n\n- **Who is this for:** New developers, new Git and GitHub users\n- **What you'll build:** You'll use a web editor to fix conflicting changes\n- **What you'll learn:** We'll introduce the tools for inspecting and resolving a merge conflict\n- **Prerequisites:** Introduction to GitHub course\n- **How long:** Less than 30 minutes\n\n### Actions Learners Will Perform in This Course\n\nIn this exercise, learners will:\n1. **Learn the causes of a merge conflict.**\n2. **Learn the tools for resolving a merge conflict.**\n3. **Learn when and how to resolve a merge conflict.**\n\nTo start the course, learners copy the exercise to their GitHub account, then give it about 20 seconds to prepare the first lesson, and refresh the page.",
